e  food is clever here nate does an amazing  job and i've worked with thousands and  thousands of young chefs over the years  and there are there's always the  standout ones and nate's one of those  standout ones can you just do this i get  to experience that first hand in the  tully kitchen where chef ko was teaching  me the ropes my garlic slicing skills  leave much to be desired  and while the chopping might have been  slow it doesn't detract from the taste  we've been seasoning from the beginning  the work is not glamorous but each dish  is lovingly prepared so basically thali  means a big dish with a lot of small  dishes on top of it it's basically our  take on indian food  and i don't think people realize how  important indian culture is in south  africa there's huge indian influence yes  there is a lot of flavors and components  that goes hand in hand together  the result a magnificent feast i'm ready  to taste it so this is ostrich carpaccio  with  so it's a spicy apple puree then we've  got some pickled mushrooms there and  then the sour onion beware there should  be a kitty as well  it is absolutely insane  another firm favorite is the pickled  fish co uses the very south african king  clip soaked in lime juice and spices  overnight  but one of tali's most popular dishes is  the humble spinach leaf transformed  under koh's expert hands into something  far more sublime yes  it says  in a temporary batter which we make  ourselves  that's one of my favorites this is  amazing i'm eating a spinach leaf who  could possibly imagine that a spinach  leaf can taste this good  cooking has always been coe's happy  place his father took early retirement  to pay for chef school every day he  would make a two-hour journey across  cape town to get there  what's it like traversing the two worlds  you live in you live in mitchell's plane  where there's poverty  gangsterism drug abuse you come here  it's a fine dining experience in many  ways i wouldn't say it's difficult bu